Resolve exactly one supplied subject node against canonical registry identities.

Do not decide ontology type, page maturity, containment, or claim ownership. Return one decision for the supplied
node ID. Choose `existing` only when the evidence establishes an exact canonical registry identity. Choose
`review_required` when the evidence cannot distinguish an existing identity from a new one, and list every
materially plausible canonical candidate. Otherwise choose `new`.

Stable-name, explicit alias or rename, and defining-history evidence can establish identity. Shared vocabulary,
participants, apparent type, or being the only available candidate cannot. Preserve a source-grounded preferred
title and aliases, explain the identity evidence, and return JSON matching the schema.
